    bin      T_dark E1       T_dark E1 err   T_dark rising
    0.5-1     607.5 +-  30.9          613.9
    1-1.5     477.3 +-  20.7          490.9
    1.5-2     421.0 +-  17.0          440.3
    2-3       373.7 +-  14.9          396.4
    3-5       312.0 +-  13.0          322.0

  full Jeans+Abel consistency (same NFW c500=4.5 + 7-piece beta):
    0.5-1: model sigma_los = 763 vs measured 952 (ratio 0.801); projection factor model sqrt(1-bA)_eff = 1.093 vs local sqrt(1-bA) = 1.108 (|d|/m = 0.013)
    1-1.5: model sigma_los = 670 vs measured 826 (ratio 0.811); projection factor model sqrt(1-bA)_eff = 0.941 vs local sqrt(1-bA) = 0.996 (|d|/m = 0.059)
    1.5-2: model sigma_los = 592 vs measured 755 (ratio 0.784); projection factor model sqrt(1-bA)_eff = 0.854 vs local sqrt(1-bA) = 0.904 (|d|/m = 0.058)
    2-3  : model sigma_los = 555 vs measured 676 (ratio 0.821); projection factor model sqrt(1-bA)_eff = 0.841 vs local sqrt(1-bA) = 0.913 (|d|/m = 0.086)
    3-5  : model sigma_los = 442 vs measured 550 (ratio 0.803); projection factor model sqrt(1-bA)_eff = 0.712 vs local sqrt(1-bA) = 0.804 (|d|/m = 0.129)
    NOTE: the absolute level (model sigma_los/measured = 0.80) carries the committed forward model's known normalization (G209 E1 chi2 = 596 on the same NFW+M500_med frame -- the E1 fit needed b_inf = 1.27 to absorb it); the inversion here uses the MEASURED sigma_los and beta directly, so it is insensitive to that normalization, and the SHAPE comparison that matters is the projection factor.

  T_dark(2-5 R500) window mean (inv-variance over the 2-3, 3-5 bins) = 333.9 +- 21.6 K = 2.88e-05 keV = 0.029 eV

