    HeCS-stack  M500_med x f_b(cosmic 0.157)  : M_b = 3.78e+13 -> sigma_eq =  585.3 km/s -> T_dark,pred = 9.17 K x (585/119.21)^2 =  221.1 K
    X-COP median M_b (G050 ingests)           : M_b = 1.08e+14 -> sigma_eq =  761.6 km/s -> T_dark,pred = 9.17 K x (762/119.21)^2 =  374.4 K
    PREDICTED T_dark (cluster class) in [221, 374] K vs MEASURED T_dark(2-5 R500) = 334 +- 22 K (z = +0.45 vs band center)
    the frame-identity check: T_dark(measured)/9.17 K = 36.4 vs (sigma_r/119.21)^2 = 35.7 (ratio 1.019; identity by construction of T = m sigma^2/k_B)

====================================================================================================
PART 3 -- THE PREDICTION: T_dark(r) shape, its relation to the beta profile, and the framework's statement about its own temperature field
====================================================================================================
  framework statement: the equilibrium phantom is ISOTHERMAL by construction (G233: P = sigma^2 rho, sigma^2 = C/2 radius-independent; the max-entropy equilibrium in the fixed baryon well G084) -- T_dark FLAT at the equilibrium value.
  measured T_dark(r): d log T/d log r = -0.279 +- 0.077  (z vs FLAT = -3.6)  [0.5-1 485 K -> 3-5 307 K across 0.7-3.9 R500]
  beta = 0 counterfactual: slope = -0.630 -- the rising beta envelope (to 0.55 at 3-5 R500) reduces the decline by 56% (sigma_r = sigma_los/sqrt(1-beta A): outward, 1-beta A < 1 raises sigma_r against the falling sigma_los)
  the equilibrium (isothermal) value at the HeCS-stack footing: T_eq = 234 K -- the measured profile is +107% above it inside 1 R500 and +31% above it in the outer bin; the window mean 334 K is +42% above the isothermal equilibrium value

